From f71500ed189cd46548d3660c853376ec85cc2bcc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tung Son Do <dosontung007@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 20:40:11 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] feat(ollama): add a live per-model context limit setting

ollama.contextLimits maps an Ollama model id, exactly as /api/tags names
it, to the largest context window the session requests for it. Every
ollama model on the native ollama-chat api is capped at its entry after
modelOverrides, so an override cannot raise it, and the native api sends
the capped window as num_ctx. A model without an entry keeps the
OLLAMA_CONTEXT_LENGTH cap. An entry that is not a positive integer up to
2^24, or a value that is not a record, is ignored instead of failing
discovery.

The session listens to the setting like extendedContext: a change,
including an edit to a watched --config overlay, rebuilds the catalog and
rebinds the active model in place. The rebind does not switch models or
reset provider sessions, and a turn in flight finishes undisturbed; the
next request carries the new num_ctx.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
